      "problem": "A number $x$ is $400%$ greater than $120.$ Find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$  \n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To find a number $400%$ *greater than* $120,$ we apply a new percentage of  \n\n$$\n100%+400%=500%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting our percentage to a decimal:  \n\n$$\n500%=\\frac{500}{100}=5\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $400%$ greater than $120,$ we multiply $120$ by $5:$  \n\n$$\n5\\cdot 120=600\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=600.$",
